  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ridge to Coast, Rain to Tap: COVID-19 response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of August 19, 2021, the Philippines Department of Health (DOH) has reported ~1.8 million cases of the disease, of which 1.65 M = recoveries and 30,881 deaths, making the Philippines the second highest number of confirmed covid cases in Southeast Asia The Philippine incidents have greatly increased in 2021, with a &gt;100% increase in the incident rate compared to 2020.

CDO is reported at critical risk. Confirmed daily cases have ranged between 100 &#x2013; 300 for the past 2 months, though a large portion of cases is never reported or confirmed due to fear of testing. OCTA Research data shows that the use of the CDO&#x2019;s intensive care facilities is at a critical risk level. Its intensive care unit utilization rate (ICUUR) has breached the 80% level mid-July and has continued to rise since then.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cagayan de Oro, Mindanao region, Philippines</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Individuals in CDO targeted sites that are eligible in accordance with The Department of Health vaccination prioritization framework .</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting vaccination efforts of the Philippine Red Cross in Cagayan de Oro (CdO)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal supporting vaccination in CdO is part of a broader PRC strategy. PRC has an excellent vaccination record and has in the past vaccinated more than a Million Children (1,044,228) against Polio and Measles in 2019/2020 by mobilizing around 3,000 trained volunteers thru 58 PRC chapters. The vaccination program forms part of larger PRC national intervention of COVID-19 testing of which the PRC has recently inaugurated a Covid -19 testing Center in Cagayan De Oro. That is capable of running a total of 2,000 tests daily an essential element of the &#x201c;testing, isolation, quarantine and vaccination&#x201d; approach mandated by the Government.

Through this intervention PRC seeks to achieve a significant contribution to its overall objective of vaccinating 1 million people through partnering with LGU&#x2019;s to facilitate the administration of the government supplied vaccine through mobile outreach buses in coordination with the LGUs. The PRC will use its vast network of volunteers for logistics, administration, awareness and education along with coordinating with local DOH/LGU medical teams for the administration of the vaccine, a modality that the PRC is rolling out nationally.</narrative>
  </description>
